※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4489

※ `⧺` joins two strings or two arrays and not one of each.  A string is not an
※ array of bytes that happens to be spelled differently: its bytes are UTF-8
※ and what it holds is characters, which is why it has no index and why this is
※ refused rather than given a meaning.

let v: u8⟦2⟧ = ⟦1u8, 2u8⟧

@[startup, impure]
fn main() → u8:
    let both: str = "ab" ⧺ v
    0u8
